Context: OpenShift Monitor Dashboard — Release Management Integration

We have an existing internal OpenShift Monitor Dashboard built with 
React/TypeScript frontend and Node.js backend. It currently monitors 
OpenShift pods, detects log errors, shows container versions, calculates 
success rates, and manages environment bookings.

We want to add a new "Release Management" tab to this dashboard that 
integrates with our BBOS Release Management Tracker on Confluence 
(page ID: 4155436802 on confluence.barcapint.com).

---

WHAT THE CONFLUENCE PAGE CONTAINS:
The Confluence page has 4 tabs:

1. Release Tracker — Monthly release table with columns:
   Month, Release Fix Version, Scope of Release, Components In-Scope 
   (IDV/CSS/ODS checkboxes), Leads, Testing Completion (SIT/Release), 
   TCR Signoff date, Walkthrough Session, CR Submit date, BLP Support 
   Alignment, BLP Scope (LP), Go/No Go, BLP Scope (PROD)

2. Month End Dates — Freeze windows per month:
   Month, Start datetime, End datetime
   (e.g. June: Start Mon 29 June 18:00, End Wed 01 July 12:00)

3. CR-2026 — Change Request log with columns:
   S.No, CR (CHG number), Details, Type, Environment, Outcome 
   (SUCCESSFUL/CANCELLED/Not implemented), Date

4. Minutes — Meeting notes with release decisions and action items

---

FEATURES WE WANT TO BUILD:

1. Release Calendar Widget
   - Show current month freeze window with live countdown
   - Color coded: Green (open), Amber (<7 days to freeze), Red (frozen)

2. Active Release Panel
   - Current and next release details
   - Scope items, component checklist (IDV/CSS/ODS), leads, key dates
   - Go/No-Go status per release

3. CR Tracker Board
   - All CHG numbers displayed as filterable board
   - Filter by: Environment (LP/PROD), Outcome, Month
   - Search by CHG number or description

4. Team Workload View
   - Per team member: how many releases owned, upcoming deadlines
   - Derived from Leads column in Release Tracker

5. Meeting Minutes Action Tracker
   - Parse minutes tab for action items
   - Show owner, status (open/closed) per action per release

6. One-Click Release Report
   - Export PDF/CSV with CR outcomes, dates, leads summary
   - Ready for stakeholder meetings

7. Go/No-Go Checklist
   - Per release checklist: Testing done, TCR Signoff, CR Submit, BLP
   - Visual completion status

8. Notifications/Alerts
   - Freeze window warnings (7 days before, 1 day before)
   - Upcoming deadline alerts for leads

